#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186297434 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064381 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "dabb3127-172e-5a68-8e27-d22057f8ea8e" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Related Rate With a Sphere: Word Problem"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f48b03f4-de1f-5518-8d7b-f0622fb8986b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296561}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f48b03f4-de1f-5518-8d7b-f0622fb8986b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296561} :answer-field/id #uuid "3697c49e-740a-5aaa-a707-4701abf7681d" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296734}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "cb5b4de1-d892-5870-99f2-1c26e26d0697" :question/math-academy-id "q-315860" :question/problem "![](images/e8/e850cd14f3b4f791c79c136d0fc799fd17fdc23eeab37e67ad2811f3ff7b6d0e.png)\n\nA snowball is melting in the sun and slowly shrinking. Determine the rate at which the surface area of the snowball is decreasing, given that the radius is decreasing at a rate of $\\frac{1}{5}\\,\\text{in/s}$ and its surface area at that moment is $100\\pi \\,{\\text{in}}^{2}.$ Do not round the answer.\n\n*Hint*: Assume that the rate of decrease is positive.\n\nThe surface area of the snowball is decreasing at a rate of \n{{field-1}} ${\\text{in}}^{2}/\\text{s}.$" :question/worked-solution "Let $r$ be the radius of the snowball and let $A$ be its surface area. Both $r$ and $A$ change with time. In particular, we are given that\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t}=-\\frac{1}{5}\\,\\text{in/s},\n$$\n\nand we want to find $\\frac{\\text{d}A}{\\text{d}t}$ when $A=100\\pi \\,{\\text{in}}^{2}.$\n\nTo start, let's write down the formula for the surface area of a sphere and then differentiate it using implicit differentiation. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =4\\pi {r}^{2} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(A) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4\\pi {r}^{2}) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(A) & =\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}r}(4\\pi {r}^{2}) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}A}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t}\\cdot 8\\pi r\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe then calculate the value of $r$ using $A=100\\pi .$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =4\\pi {r}^{2} \\\\ 100\\pi  & =4\\pi {r}^{2} \\\\ 25 & ={r}^{2} \\\\ r & =\\pm 5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince radius cannot be negative, we have $r=5.$\n\nWe now substitute $\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t}=-\\frac{1}{5}$ and $r=5$ into our expression for $\\frac{\\text{d}A}{\\text{d}t}.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}A}{\\text{d}t} & =-\\frac{1}{5}\\cdot 8\\pi \\cdot 5 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}A}{\\text{d}t} & =-8\\pi \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe conclude that the surface area of the snowball is decreasing at a rate of $8\\pi \\,{\\text{in}}^{2}\\text{/s}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186317539 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064381 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "dabb3127-172e-5a68-8e27-d22057f8ea8e" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Related Rate With a Sphere: Word Problem"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f4804743-754e-52a4-ac46-58a24afecd98" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316482}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f4804743-754e-52a4-ac46-58a24afecd98" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316482} :answer-field/id #uuid "87f30560-b7a8-5fe7-a866-713cb0a11c66" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316860}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a6cc0140-a8eb-5088-99b0-8b7a894e4ee5" :question/math-academy-id "q-344751" :question/problem "![](images/28/287add661cff085d1090295f67f87ee80eeaa3d8301ee6632ab54a812a6cd119.png)\n\nA spherical hailstone is melting uniformly, causing its radius to change at a rate of $\\frac{1}{6\\pi }\\,\\text{mm}\\text{/s}.$ If the radius at a certain moment is $15\\,\\text{mm},$ what is the rate at which the surface area is decreasing?\n\nThe surface area of the hailstone is decreasing at a rate of\n{{field-1}} ${\\text{mm}}^{2}\\text{/s}.$" :question/worked-solution "Let $r$ be the radius of the hailstone and $A$ its surface area. Both $r$ and $A$ change with time. In particular, we are given\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t}=-\\frac{1}{6\\pi }\\,\\text{mm}\\text{/s},\n$$\n\nand we want to find $\\frac{\\text{d}A}{\\text{d}t}$ when $r=15\\,\\text{mm}.$\n\nTo start, let's write down the surface area formula for the sphere and then differentiate it using implicit differentiation. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =4\\pi {r}^{2} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(A) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4\\pi {r}^{2}) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(A) & =\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}r}(4\\pi {r}^{2}) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}A}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t}8\\pi r.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow we can substitute the given information $\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t}=-\\frac{1}{6\\pi }$ and $r=15.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}A}{\\text{d}t} & =-\\frac{1}{6\\pi }\\cdot 8\\pi (15) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}A}{\\text{d}t} & =-20.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe conclude that the surface area of the hailstone is decreasing at a rate of $20{\\text{ mm}}^{2}\\text{/s}.$"}]}
